kgf 0.6
language: gemfile
sources: Gemfile

# KGF spec for Ruby Gemfile.
#
# A Gemfile is executable Ruby, so it cannot be modelled by enumerating the
# statements that happen to appear in one sample. The backbone here is a
# generic Ruby-ish statement/block structure — a statement is a call with
# arguments, and `do ... end` / `{ ... }` delimit blocks that may nest — with
# `gem`, `source` and `ruby` layered on top as the calls that carry meaning.
#
# Emits: rubyVersion, dependsOn.

=== lex
SKIP        /[ \t\\\r]+/
TOKEN NL            /\r?\n/
TOKEN Comment       /#[^\r\n]*/

# Keywords. Only the words the grammar needs structurally are keywords:
# `do`/`end` delimit blocks, and `gem`/`source`/`ruby` head the calls that
# carry semantics.
#
# NOTE: `require`, `group`, `platforms`, `git`, `path` and friends are NOT
# keywords. They appear as ordinary hash keys (`gem "x", require: false`) and
# as block-heading method names, and the lexer has no context to tell the two
# apart — a KEYWORD `require` turns the hash key into KW_require and makes
# every generic option rule fail, which is exactly what truncated this file
# at the first `require: false`.
KEYWORD KW_do         /do\b/
KEYWORD KW_end        /end\b/
KEYWORD KW_gem        /gem\b/
KEYWORD KW_source     /source\b/
KEYWORD KW_ruby       /ruby\b/
KEYWORD KW_true       /true\b/
KEYWORD KW_false      /false\b/
KEYWORD KW_nil        /nil\b/
KEYWORD KW_if         /if\b/
KEYWORD KW_unless     /unless\b/

# Literals. A symbol may be written `:name` or, as a hash key, `name:`; both
# forms appear in real Gemfiles.
TOKEN StringLit     /"([^"\\]|\\.)*"|'([^'\\]|\\.)*'/
TOKEN Symbol        /:[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*[?!]?/
TOKEN Number        /-?[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?/

# Punctuation and operators. ARROW (`=>`) must precede the generic Operator
# so a hash rocket is not split, and the operator class covers the comparison
# operators that appear in version constraints written without quotes.
TOKEN ARROW         /=>/
TOKEN LPAREN        /\(/
TOKEN RPAREN        /\)/
TOKEN LBRACE        /\{/
TOKEN RBRACE        /\}/
TOKEN LBRACKET      /\[/
TOKEN RBRACKET      /\]/
TOKEN COMMA         /,/
TOKEN COLON         /:/
TOKEN DOT           /\./
TOKEN Operator      /[!%&*+\-\/<=>?^|~]+/

# Identifiers, including the constant and variable forms.
TOKEN Ident         /[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*[?!]?/

=== grammar
GemfileContent  -> Statement*

# `Other` last: a single token of any kind, so an unfamiliar construct costs
# only itself and every `gem` line after it is still seen.
Statement       -> SourceStmt / RubyStmt / GemStmt / Block
                 / NL / Comment / Other

SourceStmt      -> KW_source Args
RubyStmt        -> KW_ruby version:StringLit

# `gem "name", "~> 1.0", require: false, group: [:test]`
GemStmt         -> KW_gem name:StringLit GemOpts?
GemOpts         -> ( COMMA Sep* OptValue )+

# Any `name ... do ... end` or `name ... { ... }` block: `group :development
# do`, `platforms :ruby do`, `source "..." do`, `git_source(:github) { |n| }`.
# Heading the rule with a generic call is what makes an unknown block kind
# (a future `gemspec do`, a conditional wrapper) parse as a block instead of
# stopping the file.
Block           -> BlockHead KW_do BlockBody KW_end
                 / BlockHead LBRACE BlockBody RBRACE
BlockHead       -> ( Ident / KW_source / KW_gem / KW_ruby / KW_if / KW_unless ) Args? BlockParams?
BlockParams     -> Operator ( Ident ( COMMA Ident )* )? Operator
BlockBody       -> Statement*

# A call's arguments, with or without parentheses.
Args            -> LPAREN Sep* ArgList? RPAREN / ArgList
ArgList         -> OptValue ( Sep* COMMA Sep* OptValue )*

# An argument or option: a hash entry in either Ruby syntax, or a bare value.
OptValue        -> HashEntry / Value
HashEntry       -> Symbol ARROW Sep* Value
                 / HashKey COLON Sep* Value
# A hash key written `name:` may be any identifier, including one that is
# also a keyword elsewhere (`source:`, `gem:`, `if:`).
HashKey         -> Ident / KW_source / KW_gem / KW_ruby / KW_do / KW_end
                 / KW_if / KW_unless / KW_true / KW_false / KW_nil

Value           -> StringLit / Symbol / Number / KW_true / KW_false / KW_nil
                 / HashLit / ArrayLit / Call / Ident

Call            -> Ident LPAREN Sep* ArgList? RPAREN / Ident DOT Ident Args?
HashLit         -> LBRACE Sep* ( OptValue ( Sep* COMMA Sep* OptValue )* ( Sep* COMMA )? )? Sep* RBRACE
ArrayLit        -> LBRACKET Sep* ( Value ( Sep* COMMA Sep* Value )* ( Sep* COMMA )? )? Sep* RBRACKET

Sep             -> NL / Comment

Other           -> StringLit / Symbol / Number / Ident / Operator
                 / KW_true / KW_false / KW_nil / KW_if / KW_unless
                 / KW_source / KW_gem / KW_ruby / KW_do / KW_end
                 / COMMA / COLON / DOT / ARROW
                 / LPAREN / RPAREN / LBRACE / RBRACE / LBRACKET / RBRACKET

=== attrs
on SourceStmt: note fieldKey payload="source"
on RubyStmt:   note fieldKey payload="ruby"

=== semantics
on RubyStmt {
  let ver = stripQuotes($version)
  edge rubyVersion from $file to ver attrs obj("raw", $version)
}
on GemStmt {
  let name = stripQuotes($name)
  edge dependsOn from $file to concat("rubygems:", name) attrs obj("dep_kind", "runtime")
}

=== features
content_type: config

=== resolver
relative_prefixes:
exts: Gemfile
indexes:
bare_prefix: rubygems:
module_path_style: hyphen
